vertices.",
 "\n"
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"62413299-2637-4dec-af17-ef6d68d4c1cd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A fibered graph is a graph ",
 StyleBox["E", "TI"],
 " with a map ",
 StyleBox["\[Pi]", "TI"],
 " on its vertices. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraFiberedGraphQ"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraFiberedGraphQ", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "7109b52c-d64e-44f0-950d-e093a4777381"],
 " tests only that ",
 StyleBox["\[Pi]", "TI"],
 " is defined on every vertex of ",
 StyleBox["E", "TI"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"b1e1fade-e04f-482a-ba3b-3f0bbf2708ad"],

Cell["\<\
The total graph must be finite, simple, undirected, unweighted and without \
edge tags. The projection is an association with one key for each vertex, or \
a function.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"f92e0b98-ff67-43c9-ada3-b1114c23319a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "No further condition is tested. Fibers of different sizes, vertical edges \
and vertices without lifts are allowed; ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraFibrationQ"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraFibrationQ", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "a9f5062b-4fd7-4fcc-8a33-30bdb5f7a25f"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraFiberBundleQ"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraFiberBundleQ", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "298acfd1-d844-4034-81aa-c0a7b11cc5f6"],
 " test those."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"fecf0630-a12e-4add-8651-4646068a5ed9"],

Cell["Accepted heads:", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"478095dc-1d8b-4b6d-9140-dc1b1a834002"],

